  "question": {
    "text": "Arrange the following compounds in order of decreasing acidity :<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0372_27839de9550e.jpg\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 214px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mtext>III</mtext> <mo>&#62;</mo> <mtext>I</mtext> <mo>&#62;</mo> <mtext>II</mtext> <mo>&#62;</mo> <mtext>IV</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mrow>  <mtext>IV</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>III</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>I</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>II</mtext></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mtext>II</mtext> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mtext>IV</mtext> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mtext>I</mtext> <mo>&gt;</mo> <mtext>III</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mrow>  <mtext>I</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>II</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>III</mtext>  <mo>&gt;</mo>  <mtext>IV</mtext></mrow></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Acidity is directly proportional to conjugated base stability.<br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"182\" src=\"assets\\st0372_f3026d9ee227.jpg\" width=\"444\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"172\" src=\"assets\\st0372_0fc84daa829c.jpg\" width=\"469\" /><br /><br />Stability order of conjugate bases is III &gt; I &gt; II &gt; IV<br /><br />Conjugate base in I is stabilised by - I &gt; + M<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate&nbsp;</span>base in II is destabilised by + I and hyperconjugation.<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">&nbsp;</span> base in III is stabilised by strong withdrawing effect of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> by - I &amp; - M effect.<br /><br /><span style=\"font-size: 12.7272720336914px; line-height: 20.8000011444092px;\">Conjugate&nbsp;</span>base in IV is destabilised by + M effect of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>acidic</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>character</mi><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8733;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mtext>&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;&#8201;</mtext><mo>&#8733;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>HC</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math><br /><br />Electron releasing group (i.e +I effect, +M) decreases the acidic strength&nbsp;<br />Electron withdrawing group (i.e -I effect,-M) increases acidic strength.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0372_e406818230ec.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 160px;\" /><br />&nbsp;"
  }
}